  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "Nothing new — just faster",
      "title_pl": "Nic nowego — tylko szybciej",
      "body": "Every past form you have met is the same machine: the verb, then -ł-, then a person ending. The ending does two jobs at once — it says who, and it says male or female. This unit only trains the choosing.",
      "body_pl": "Czasownik + -ł- + końcówka. Kto? Mężczyzna czy kobieta?",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Who",
          "Ending",
          "być",
          "robić"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "ja — I (man)",
            "-em",
            "byłem",
            "robiłem"
          ],
          [
            "ja — I (woman)",
            "-am",
            "byłam",
            "robiłam"
          ],
          [
            "ty — you (to a man)",
            "-eś",
            "byłeś",
            "robiłeś"
          ],
          [
            "ty — you (to a woman)",
            "-aś",
            "byłaś",
            "robiłaś"
          ],
          [
            "on — he",
            "no ending",
            "był",
            "robił"
          ],
          [
            "ona — she",
            "-a",
            "była",
            "robiła"
          ],
          [
            "ono — it",
            "-o",
            "było",
            "robiło"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The two mistakes this gym kills",
      "title_pl": "Dwa błędy",
      "body": "Almost every past-tense error is one of these four. Read the row, then the reason.",
      "body_pl": "Kto mówi? Jaki rodzaj?",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Situation",
          "Wrong",
          "Right",
          "Reason"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "a man says: I was",
            "byłam",
            "byłem",
            "-em is the man's I-ending"
          ],
          [
            "you ask a woman: were you?",
            "byłeś",
            "byłaś",
            "-aś is the woman's you-ending"
          ],
          [
            "same person, wrong slot",
            "byłem? (asking)",
            "byłeś?",
            "-em = I, -eś = you"
          ],
          [
            "a feminine noun as subject",
            "mama robił",
            "mama robiła",
            "the noun's gender picks the verb"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Wczoraj",
      "title_pl": "Wczoraj",
      "body": "From here on nothing announces the past — wczoraj (yesterday) sets the scene and the verb carries the rest. The bracket tells you the gender you need: (m) a man speaking or spoken to, (f) a woman.",
      "body_pl": "Wczoraj — reszta jest w czasowniku.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "Yesterday I was at work. (m)",
          "pl": "Wczoraj byłem w pracy."
        },
        {
          "en": "Yesterday I was at work. (f)",
          "pl": "Wczoraj byłam w pracy."
        },
        {
          "en": "Yesterday Mum was drinking coffee.",
          "pl": "Wczoraj mama piła kawę."
        },
        {
          "en": "Yesterday Dad was working at home.",
          "pl": "Wczoraj tata pracował w domu."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
